             decimal prefix (kB, MB, ..) or binary prefix (kiB, MiB, ..), or can be specified \
             using a hex number. The short option '-l' can be used as an alias.\nExamples: \
             --length=64, --length=4KiB, --length=0xff",
        );

    let skip = Arg::new("skip")
        .short('s')
        .long("skip")
        .value_name("N")
        .help(
            "Skip the first N bytes of the input. The N argument can also include a unit (see \
             `--length` for details).\nA negative value is valid and will seek from the end of \
             the file.",
